</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">What it costs — and what it saves</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Paying for a concept phase without seeing anything is hard. The objection is fair, and the answer to it is not a promise but a calculation: rounds of revisions are the most expensive item in communication projects. They arise when drafts are discussed for which there is no rationale — then hierarchy takes the place of argument, and compromise the place of decision.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Once a concept exists, the discussion moves one level forward: you argue about assumptions, not about taste. That argument is shorter because it can be settled — and it takes place before production, not after.</p>
</section>

